RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 0 RMLoad <IXFS$HardDisc4>.TestBed.Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0 RMLoad <IXFS$HardDisc4>.TestBed.Modules.PThrTicker
RMEnsure VFPSupport 0 RMLoad <IXFS$HardDisc4>.TestBed.Modules.VFPSupport
| ARMEABISupport: !System's if it has one, else the image's (GCCSDK's 1.05)
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 IfThere System:Modules.ARMEABISupport Then RMLoad System:Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 RMLoad <IXFS$HardDisc4>.TestBed.Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure BASICVFP 0 RMLoad <IXFS$HardDisc4>.TestBed.Modules.BASICVFP
| MbufManager (DCI4 network buffers): in every RISC OS 5 ROM, and in this
| one from 5.31-7; !Omni's LanManFS and Access need it
RMEnsure MbufManager 0 RMLoad <IXFS$HardDisc4>.TestBed.Modules.MbufRes
RMEnsure MbufManager 0 RMLoad <IXFS$HardDisc4>.TestBed.Modules.MManager
| character set conversion: RISC OS Open's Iconv is in !System (from its
| Raspberry Pi distribution); as on a RISC OS install it's loaded when a
| program first needs it (UnixLib does RMEnsure Iconv ... RMLoad
| System:Modules.Iconv), by when !Unicode, which it needs, is set up.
| the scroll wheel: rol-fb sends it as key numbers &1F0-&1F3
RMEnsure KVMWheel 0 RMLoad <IXFS$HardDisc4>.TestBed.Modules.KVMWheel
| which way it scrolls: Configure, Scroll wheel (*KVMWheel Reverse|Normal)
IfThere Choices:KVMWheel Then /Choices:KVMWheel
| and RISC OS Open's WindowScroll scrolls windows with it (its task starts
| with the desktop; *WimpScroll configures it)
RMEnsure WindowScroll 0 RMLoad <IXFS$HardDisc4>.TestBed.Modules.WindowScroll
| sound: LinuxAudio is an audio device for RISC OS Open's SoundDMA (in the
| ROM, which has no other) and sends the sound to Linux (rol-snd plays it);
| SoundControl (the mixer: *MixVolume, Configure's volume) and SharedSound
| are RISC OS Open's too. SoundDMA is started again to find the device,
| then the ROM's other sound modules, to register with it.
RMEnsure LinuxAudio 0 RMLoad <IXFS$HardDisc4>.TestBed.Modules.LinuxAudio
RMEnsure SoundControl 0 RMLoad <IXFS$HardDisc4>.TestBed.Modules.SoundControl
RMReInit SoundDMA
RMReInit SoundChannels
RMReInit SoundScheduler
RMReInit WaveSynth
RMReInit StringLib
RMReInit Percussion
RMEnsure SharedSound 0 RMLoad <IXFS$HardDisc4>.TestBed.Modules.SharedSound
| *Linux: runs Linux commands (the image's rol-cmd runs them; Updates uses it)
RMEnsure LinuxShell 0 RMLoad <IXFS$HardDisc4>.TestBed.Modules.LinuxShell
| *IXRun goes through *LinuxUser: rol-cmd runs the command (through the
| shell, so the path is searched) as RISC OS's own Linux user, with no
| password, protected or not (IXSupport's own needs Linux programs and a
| terminal in RISC OS's view of the files, which protected RISC OS hasn't)
Set Alias$IXRun LinuxUser %%*0
| USBDriver: RISC OS's USB device interface on Linux's usbfs, for the USB devices
| Linux has no driver for (phones, cameras: PDFS)
RMEnsure USBDriver 0 RMLoad <IXFS$HardDisc4>.TestBed.Modules.USBDriver
| LinuxCodec: Linux's video decoders (VideoCore's H.264 on a Pi 3 or 4) for
| RISC OS programs; on machines without one, LinuxCodec_Open says so and
| programs decode in software
RMEnsure LinuxCodec 0 RMLoad <IXFS$HardDisc4>.TestBed.Codec.LinuxCodec
| VideoCore stand-ins (VCHIQ, BCMSupport, PCI over Linux's /dev/vchiq and
| /dev/vcio): ReelHWAccel's H.264 decoding and encoding for Reel, Matinee
| and FFmpeg on a Pi 3 or 4. Only where Linux has a VideoCore.
IfThere IXFS:$.dev.vchiq Then Obey <IXFS$HardDisc4>.TestBed.Codec.LoadVC
